From: REG-Linux <cjom@reglinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] outer.hh: include <cstdint> for uintptr_t

GCC 16's libstdc++ no longer pulls <cstdint> in through <cstddef>, so
UserSettings.cc fails with "'uintptr_t' does not name a type".

Signed-off-by: REG-Linux <cjom@reglinux.org>
---
--- a/src/utils/outer.hh
+++ b/src/utils/outer.hh
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 #define OUTER_HH
 
 #include <cstddef>
+#include <cstdint>
 
 // Example usage:
 //   class Foo {
